# Build DYD 2026 Android APK (Windows)

Flutter release APK for sideloading (testing / sharing). The Android project is
configured to sign release builds with the **debug keystore** so you do not need
a Play Store signing key yet. For Play Store production, add a release keystore
in `android/app/build.gradle.kts` later.

---

## Prerequisites (one-time)

1. **Flutter** at `C:\flutter` (no spaces in path).
   - Check: `C:\flutter\bin\flutter.bat doctor`
2. **JDK 17** — this repo expects:
   - `C:\Program Files\Microsoft\jdk-17.0.19.10-hotspot`
   - Install if missing: `winget install Microsoft.OpenJDK.17`
3. **Android SDK** (Android Studio or command-line tools).
   - Accept licenses: `flutter doctor --android-licenses`
4. **Project folder** — open a terminal in:
   - `C:\Users\Kent Veloso\Desktop\DEV PROJECTS\dyd2026`

---

## Option A — Recommended (PowerShell script)

From **PowerShell**, in the project root:

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\Kent Veloso\Desktop\DEV PROJECTS\dyd2026"
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\build_android.ps1
```

When it finishes, the APK path is printed. Default output:

`build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-release.apk`

---

## Option B — Run the same steps manually in terminal

Copy and paste this block in **PowerShell** (adjust `JdkHome` if your JDK path differs):

```powershell
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"

$FlutterBin = "C:\flutter\bin"
$JdkHome = "C:\Program Files\Microsoft\jdk-17.0.19.10-hotspot"
$ProjectRoot = "C:\Users\Kent Veloso\Desktop\DEV PROJECTS\dyd2026"

$env:Path = "$FlutterBin;$JdkHome\bin;$env:Path"
$env:JAVA_HOME = $JdkHome

Set-Location $ProjectRoot

& "$FlutterBin\flutter.bat" pub get
& "$FlutterBin\flutter.bat" build apk --release

$apk = Join-Path $ProjectRoot "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-release.apk"
Write-Host "APK ready: $apk"
```

